kanban-md: `source <(kanban-md completion bash)`, `kanban-md completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_kanban-md"`, `kanban-md completion fish | source`. karr has nothing; with 30 commands and their option names an interactive user types blind.

## What to build

`karr completion bash|zsh|fish` printing a static completion script generated from the command table in App::karr and each command's options (MooX::Options exposes them): command names, hyphenated option names and, where cheap, the fixed value lists (`--sort`, default priorities). Dynamic completion of task ids is optional. No new runtime dependency unless it is already in cpanfile. Document in README (Installation) and `karr --help`. Changes entry.

Pointers: @COMMANDS and %COMMAND_ALIASES in lib/App/karr.pm are the command table; MooX::Options exposes each command class's declared options (its _options_data), which is where the hyphenated names and value types come from. Keep the generated script static: no karr call at completion time.

